ActualOutput_Q2:
Capacity building Provincial Tourism Office, Municipality, and Tourism Stakeholders was conducted as follows:
• Mthatha: 6, 7 and 8 August 2024;
• Komani: 13, 14 and 15 August 2024.

PrelimaryAudited_Summary2:
Four Joint tourist safety awareness sessions were conducted as follows:
•	Eastern Cape - 13 to June 2024 in Mthatha;
•	KwaZulu-Natal - 20 to 22 August 2024 in Manguzi;
•	North West - 5 to 7 November 2024 in Sun City.
•	Gauteng - 4 to 6 March 2025 in Mogale City Local Municipality.

ActualOutput_Q3:
Achieved

•	Participation by Traditional Leaders in the Eastern Seaboard Ministerial Engagement Session facilitated whereby the Minister consulted with key stakeholders on the ESD programme;
•	Inputs were received on the establishment of the Special Purpose Vehicle (SPV) for the ESD;
•	 A meeting with MISA and MIVJ was held on 22/11/2024 were the details of the Proposed ESD Traditional Leader’s Summit were discussed. Subsequently, MIJV circulated the draft Concept note for the summit. The meeting also  agreed to facilitate the participation by Traditional Leaders in the ESD Project Management Committee (PMC) by scheduling briefing sessions with the affected Kingships
